 "final_text_tail": "update_deltas is sized by the number of columns (`shape[-1] - 1`), and the numba kernel indexes it with `deltas[j - 1]`, where `j` is the column. For a single column, `update_deltas` is empty, so the lookup fails to apply the decay. The fix touches both the delta construction and the kernel's indexing.\n\n{\"files\": [\"pandas/core/window/ewm.py\", \"pandas/core/window/online.py\"], \"functions\": [\"OnlineExponentialMovingWindow.mean\", \"generate_online_numba_ewma_func.online_ewma\", \"EWMMeanState.run_ewm\"]}",
